<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    @* Declared here as well as in the stylesheet, because this is the earliest point
       a browser — or an extension deciding whether a site needs its help — can read
       it. AniQueue ships a full dark palette, so anything re-theming it on top is
       redoing work, and in one measured case broke the page outright (§9). *@
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark" />
    <base href="/" />
    @* Without an explicit icon, browsers probe /favicon.ico on every page load.
       That 404s, and the 404 handler re-executes the whole app — returning a 4.6 KB
       HTML page in answer to a request for an icon. *@
    <link rel="icon" href="@Assets["favicon.svg"]" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <ResourcePreloader />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["app.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["AniQueue.Web.styles.css"]" />
    <ImportMap />
    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
</head>

<body>
    <Routes @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
    <ReconnectModal />
    <script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
</body>

</html>
